# 3 readings by claude-opus-5-5, compared
hobbes-leviathan-1.md:1: argue/readings: S3 is read 2 ways: hobbes-leviathan-1.logic.r2 and hobbes-leviathan-1.logic.r2.2 have "unjust_contrary_law" and "unjust_contrary_law → laws_rules_just"; hobbes-leviathan-1.logic.r2.3 has "unjust_contrary_law"; they differ when only "nothing is reputed unjust that is not contrary to some law" is true, which the second allows
hobbes-leviathan-1.md:1: argue/answered: S3: answered no, which keeps hobbes-leviathan-1.logic.r2 and hobbes-leviathan-1.logic.r2.2, to: Suppose "nothing is reputed unjust that is not contrary to some law" is true and "laws are the rules of just and unjust" is false. Is S3, "As also, that Lawes are the Rules of Just, and Unjust; nothing being reputed Unjust, that is not contrary to some Law.", true then?
hobbes-leviathan-1.md:1: argue/readings: S4 is read 2 ways: hobbes-leviathan-1.logic.r2 and hobbes-leviathan-1.logic.r2.2 have "subjection_cw_only" and "subjection_cw_only → only_cw_makes_laws" and "obey_needs_signs" and "obey_needs_signs → commands_signified"; hobbes-leviathan-1.logic.r2.3 has "subjection_cw_only" and "obey_needs_signs"; they differ when only "our subjection is to the common-wealth only", "none can make laws but the common-wealth" and "a man knows not otherwise (than by sufficient signs) how to obey commands" are true, which the second allows
hobbes-leviathan-1.md:1: argue/answered: S4: answered no, which keeps hobbes-leviathan-1.logic.r2 and hobbes-leviathan-1.logic.r2.2, to: Suppose "our subjection is to the common-wealth only", "none can make laws but the common-wealth" and "a man knows not otherwise (than by sufficient signs) how to obey commands" are true and "commands are to be signified by sufficient signs" is false. Is S4, "Likewise, that none can make Lawes but the Common-wealth; because our Subjection is to the Common-wealth only: and that Commands, are to be signified by sufficient Signs; because a man knows not otherwise how to obey them.", true then?
hobbes-leviathan-1.logic.r2: argue/readings: what the text leaves unstated is read 2 ways: hobbes-leviathan-1.logic.r2 and hobbes-leviathan-1.logic.r2.2 have "laws_to_addressees ∧ laws_rules_just ∧ only_cw_makes_laws ∧ commands_signified → definition_evident" and "definition_evident → O acknowledge_deductions"; hobbes-leviathan-1.logic.r2.3 has "unjust_contrary_law → laws_rules_just" and "subjection_cw_only → only_cw_makes_laws" and "obey_needs_signs → commands_signified" and "laws_to_addressees ∧ laws_rules_just ∧ only_cw_makes_laws ∧ commands_signified → definition_evident" and "definition_evident → O acknowledge_deductions"; they differ when only "laws are laws to every one to whom the command is directed, and to none else", "nothing is reputed unjust that is not contrary to some law", "laws are the rules of just and unjust", "our subjection is to the common-wealth only", "none can make laws but the common-wealth", "a man knows not otherwise (than by sufficient signs) how to obey commands", "in the definition there is nothing that is not at first sight evident", "it ought to be that whatsoever can from this definition by necessary consequence be deduced is acknowledged for truth" and "it ought to be that whatsoever can from this definition by necessary consequence be deduced is acknowledged for truth" are true, which the first allows
